---
description: Operate the business-document ingestion control layer safely and audibly.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `SKILL.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and the relevant phase reference before work. Use
`HANDOFF.md` for current state. Read `references/artifact-contracts.md` before
changing an interface, workbook, output, or runbook.

Preserve source pages and original values; corrections are append-only
amendments. Emit every failure or uncertainty as an explicit exception. Require
genuinely independent evidence for consensus and keep provider confidence
non-decisional. Arithmetic, attribution, completeness, and final review are
separate gates. LLM output, mappings, grouping, client workbook imports, and
review reduction remain proposals until authorized changes are applied and the
affected controls are rerun.

Use repository scripts and new no-clobber output paths. Every environment
setting is in `references/runtime-configuration.md`; every CLI is indexed in
`references/command-line-reference.md`, fully enumerated in
`references/cli-help-catalogue.md`, and defined exactly by its `--help`.
Before client records, follow `docs/CLIENT_USER_GUIDE.md`. Before Google-backed
work, run `scripts/reauthorize_google.py` and keep credentials external.

Only approved, provenance-linked, review-clear facts enter canonical retrieval
or target staging. Additional production OCR/HTR providers, golden-set accuracy,
detector deployment, target CRM delivery, and public tenant-isolated retrieval
remain client-authorized integrations.

To operate a run against real documents rather than change the repository, use
`skills/business-doc-operations/SKILL.md`. Its lane table maps every command to
its phase and says whether the lane is optional or disabled by default, and it
routes to task guides: `tasks/setup.md` for Phase 0 settings and file placement,
`tasks/run-pipeline.md` for the ordered sequence through 4Q,
`tasks/extraction.md` for Phase 3 reading, `tasks/cross-checking.md` for
corroboration and independent verification, `tasks/handwriting.md` for Phase 3H,
`tasks/business-controls.md` for Phases 3A/4/4Q, `tasks/evidence-graph.md` for
the graph and relationship lanes, `tasks/client-review-lane.md` for turning any
blocked control into a client-answerable pack, `tasks/review-reduction.md` for
the proposal-only queue reduction, `tasks/client-review.md` for the workbook,
`tasks/monitor.md` for progress and spend, `tasks/deliver.md` for Phases 5/6,
`tasks/troubleshooting.md` for any refusal, `tasks/maintenance.md` for the
repository gates, and `tasks/subagents.md` before delegating. Do not advance past
a failed phase exit condition; say what is blocking instead.

For approved Phase 6 facts, use `skills/mcp-api-operations/SKILL.md` for local
or remote MCP and REST API setup, deployment acceptance, client connection,
CRM queries/reports/exports, monitoring, rebuild, and shutdown. Never start or
register a surface before its activation and deployment-authorization gates.

For separately authorized new image intake, use `skills/record-intake/SKILL.md`
and `references/visual-ingestion.md`. The optional journal retains sources and
proposals only. Require real-byte transfer; never invent base64 or treat a
pending proposal as published. The local source-only export utility can prepare
images for normal profiling/intake; it never promotes proposal values or mutates
canonical records. Preserve its originals, hash receipt and review exceptions.

After any change under `scripts/`, run `python scripts/agent_surface_check.py`.
It verifies that every command named in an instruction surface still exists and
is indexed, so a rename cannot leave these instructions stale.

Run the full gate in `AGENTS.md`. Regenerate, render, and visually inspect every
changed tracked PDF. Read `BRANCHING.md` before branch operations.

Approvals are keyed to template fingerprints derived from the emitted label set,
so re-extraction orphans every prior approval: check fingerprint overlap before
sending proposals for approval and before running any mapping-dependent control.
Resolve a lane's model from its own lane setting, and treat the retained raw
response as the authority over any configuration file. Supply table lanes with
independent evidence or their conditional buddy check is unavailable rather than
unnecessary. Never resume across a changed model or reasoning effort. Hand the
gate every review-bearing artifact; a finding you do not pass in is absent from
the queue, the grouping, and the client pack. Measure with the code's own
helpers over the model's emitted output only, on matched page sets -- a retained
record may echo the prompt, and a rate over a different population is not a
comparison.

**Reconcile from retained artifacts before re-reading anything.** Every provider
response is kept under `RUN/providers/raw/`, and the independent non-LLM
extractor keeps the *whole page* rather than the fields the schema named, so a
value the pipeline dropped is usually still on disk with its layout. Grep the
retained responses for the column heading, find a printed join key the records
already carry, and re-extract only when that fails -- affected pages only,
amendment recorded first. A recovered value is single-extractor evidence, never
vendor agreement.

**Agreement is not accuracy.** A correct transcription filed under the wrong
field is what two vendors agree on, because both read the page correctly and
both assumed the same thing about the column. A field the schema never defines
is a field engines guess at, and a printed column with no field at all goes
into whichever field looks closest. Check `FIELD_DEFINITIONS` coverage and the
document's own arithmetic. Carry a value that fails such a check and label it;
never repair a reading to make it agree, and never drop a row for failing one.

Full checklist: `skills/business-doc-operations/tasks/lane-checklist.md`.
